    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26huGPNqycd8FTyQhZW4n9J)_\n\n## Cause\n`sp-dashboard--scan-file` (added in #213) reads each changed agenda file with `insert-file-contents` in a `with-temp-buffer`, then sets `buffer-file-name`. The insert leaves the buffer modified, so when `with-temp-buffer` kills it Emacs asks `Buffer  *temp*-123456 modified; kill anyway?`, once per scanned file. `--debug-init` shows nothing because it is a prompt, not an error. Before #213 the files were visited through `org-map-entries` on file lists, with no such buffer.\n\n## Fix\nMark the buffer unmodified before setting `buffer-file-name` and again after `org-mode`. Module, tangled doc, CHANGELOG and one ERT test updated.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD54mRzhA4eVYmmuYN)_",
